#! great cistern - a tin-lined belly sunk to its rim in the earth
#! Sunk to the rim, so there is no vessel to draw: what shows is the mouth, the
#! ring of stone holding it, and the water. The stone ring is stipple with one
#! lit upper edge; the water is solid body with a single highlight glint, which
#! is what stops the whole thing reading as a boulder.
